{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And of Levi he said: Your perfection and your instruction, for your holy man, etc.</b> Since Jacob cursed him and said: ״אָרוּר אַפָּם כִּי עָז וְעֶבְרָתָם כִּי קָשָׁתָה״ (Genesis 49:7), and perhaps from that curse Moses stumbled through his anger when he said: ״שִׁמְעוּ נָא הַמּוֹרִים״ (Numbers 20:10). Therefore Moses said that the words of Jacob had already been fulfilled upon him, and would that there be no more such a thing in the tribe of Levi, for they are instructors who give instruction in Israel, and every anger leads to error. Therefore Moses prayed and said of Levi: ״Your perfection and your instruction for your holy man,״ that You would illuminate for him the path so that he would not stumble again through his anger. And if you should say: but what shall I do about the words of father Jacob the patriarch, who cursed their anger? — of this he said: ״אֲשֶׁר נִסִּיתוֹ בְּמַסָּה״ etc. (Deuteronomy 33:8), for there the curse had already been fulfilled, and from now on the year and its curses shall be consumed. And what happened to Moses would serve as atonement for the entire tribe, for it is enough that the words of the patriarch were fulfilled, and such things shall never happen again, for that tribe is one which gives instruction in Israel."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:16:28.873013623Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}